      "explain": "The 1993 study reported the best violinists had accumulated about 7,410 hours of solitary practice by 18, versus 3,420 for future teachers, and over 10,000 by 20; those are averages, and Ericsson himself rejected the threshold reading. Macnamara, Hambrick and Oswald (2014) found practice explains 26% of performance variance in games, 21% in music, 18% in sports, 4% in education and under 1% in professions. Ericsson (2016) replied that the meta-analysis counted almost any practice, not deliberate practice as defined. The preregistered replication with 39 Cleveland violinists (Macnamara and Maitra 2019) found the best had practised less than the good (8,224 vs 9,844 hours by 18), with practice explaining 26% of variance rather than the original 48%. That is a live, contested empirical question. Options A and B each pick a side and call it settled. Option D overstates both ends."
